H8100.definition:
feminine of H8088 (שֵׁמַע); annunciation;
Shimath, an Ammonitess
KJV: Shimath.

H8101.definition:
patronymically from H8093 (שִׁמְעָה);
a Shimathite (collectively) or descendants of Shimah
KJV: Shimeathites.

H8102.definition:
from an unused root meaning to emit a sound;
an inkling
KJV: a little.

H8103.definition:
feminine of H8102 (שֶׁמֶץ);
scornful whispering (of hostile spectators)
KJV: shame.

H8104.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to hedge about (as with thorns), i.e. guard; generally, to protect, attend to, etc.
KJV: beward, be circumspect, take heed (to self), keep(-er, self), mark, look narrowly, observe, preserve, regard, reserve, save (self), sure, (that lay) wait (for), watch(-man).

H8105.definition:
from H8104 (שָׁמַר);
something preserved, i.e. the settlings (plural only) of wine
KJV: dregs, (wines on the) lees.

H8106.definition:
the same as H8105 (שֶׁמֶר);
Shemer, the name of three Israelites
KJV: Shamer, Shemer.

H8107.definition:
from H8104 (שָׁמַר);
an observance
KJV: [idiom] be (much) observed.

H8108.definition:
feminine of an unused noun from H8104 (שָׁמַר) meaning a guard;
watchfulness
KJV: watch.

H8109.definition:
feminine of passive participle of H8104 (שָׁמַר);
something guarded, i.e. an eye-lid
KJV: waking.

H8110.definition:
from H8105 (שֶׁמֶר) in its original sense; guardianship;
Shimron, the name of an Israelite and of a place in Palestine
KJV: Shimron.

H8111.definition:
from the active participle of H8104 (שָׁמַר); watch-station;
Shomeron, a place in Palestine
KJV: Samaria.

H8112.definition:
from H8110 (שִׁמְרוֹן) and a derivative of H4754 (מָרָא); guard of lashing;
Shimron-Meron, a place in Palestine
KJV: Shimon-meron.

H8113.definition:
from H8105 (שֶׁמֶר) in its original sense; watchful;
Shimri, the name of four Israelites
KJV: Shimri.

H8114.definition:
or שְׁמַרְיָהוּ; from H8104 (שָׁמַר) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has guarded;
Shemarjah, the name of four Israelites
KJV: Shamariah, Shemariah.

H8115.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H8111 (שֹׁמְרוֹן);
Shomrain, a place in Palestine
KJV: Samaria.

H8116.definition:
feminine of H8113 (שִׁמְרִי); female guard;
Shimrith, a Moabitess
KJV: Shimrith.

H8117.definition:
patronymically from H8110 (שִׁמְרוֹן);
a Shimronite (collectively) or descendants of Shimron
KJV: Shimronites.

H8118.definition:
patrial from H8111 (שֹׁמְרוֹן);
a Shomeronite (collectively) or inhabitants of Shomeron
KJV: Samaritans.

H8119.definition:
from H8104 (שָׁמַר); guardship;
Shimrath, an Israelite
KJV: Shimrath.

H8120.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to the root of H8121 (שֶׁמֶשׁ) through the idea of activity implied in day-light;
to serve
KJV: minister.

H8121.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be brilliant;
the sun; by implication, the east; figuratively, a ray, i.e. (architectural) a notched battlement
KJV: [phrase] east side(-ward), sun (rising), [phrase] west(-ward), window. See also H1053 (בֵּית שֶׁמֶשׁ).

H8122.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H8121 (שֶׁמֶשׁ);
the sun
KJV: sun.

H8123.definition:
from H8121 (שֶׁמֶשׁ); sunlight;
Shimshon, an Israelite
KJV: Samson.

H8124.definition:
(Aramaic) from H8122 (שֶׁמֶשׁ); sunny;
Shimshai, a Samaritan
KJV: Shimshai.

H8125.definition:
apparently from H8121 (שֶׁמֶשׁ); sunlike;
Shamsherai, an Israelite
KJV: Shamsherai.

H8126.definition:
patronymically from an unused name from H7762 (שׁוּם) probably meaning garlic-smell;
a Shumathite (collectively) or descendants of Shumah
KJV: Shumathites.

H8127.definition:
from H8150 (שָׁנַן); compare  H8143 (שֶׁנְהַבִּים)
a tooth (as sharp); specifically  ivory; figuratively, a cliff
KJV: crag, [idiom] forefront, ivory, [idiom] sharp, tooth.

H8128.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H8127 (שֵׁן);
a tooth
KJV: tooth.

H8129.definition:
the same as H8127 (שֵׁן); crag;
Shen, a place in Palestine
KJV: Shen.

H8130.definition:
a primitive root;
to hate (personally)
KJV: enemy, foe, (be) hate(-ful, -r), odious, [idiom] utterly.

H8131.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H8130 (שָׂנֵא)
{to hate (personally)}
KJV: hate.

H8132.definition:
a primitive root;
to alter
KJV: change.

H8133.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H8132 (שָׁנָא)
{to alter}
KJV: alter, change, (be) diverse.

H8134.definition:
probably from H8132 (שָׁנָא) and H1 (אָב); a father has turned;
Shinab, a Canaanite
KJV: Shinab.

H8135.definition:
from H8130 (שָׂנֵא);
hate
KJV: [phrase] exceedingly, hate(-ful, -red).

H8136.definition:
from H8132 (שָׁנָא);
change, i.e. repetition
KJV: [idiom] angels.

H8137.definition:
apparently of Babylonian origin;
Shenatstsar, an Israelite
KJV: Senazar.

H8138.definition:
a primitive root;
to fold, i.e. duplicate (literally or figuratively); by implication, to transmute (transitive or intransitive)
KJV: do (speak, strike) again, alter, double, (be given to) change, disguise, (be) diverse, pervert, prefer, repeat, return, do the second time.

H8140.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H8141 (שָׁנֶה)
{a year (as a revolution of time)}
KJV: year.

H8141.definition:
(in plural or (feminine) שָׁנָה; from H8138 (שָׁנָה);
a year (as a revolution of time)
KJV: [phrase] whole age, [idiom] long, [phrase] old, year([idiom] -ly).

H8142.definition:
or שֵׁנָא; (Psalm 127:2), from H3462 (יָשֵׁן);
sleep
KJV: sleep.

H8143.definition:
from H8127 (שֵׁן) and the plural apparently of a foreign word;
probably, tooth of elephants, i.e. ivory tusk
KJV: ivory.

H8144.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
crimson, properly, the insect or its color, also stuff dyed with it
KJV: crimson, scarlet (thread).

H8145.definition:
from H8138 (שָׁנָה);
properly, double, i.e. second; also adverbially, again
KJV: again, either (of them), (an-) other, second (time).

H8147.definition:
dual of H8145 (שֵׁנִי); feminine שְׁתַּיִם;
two; also (as ordinal) twofold
KJV: both, couple, double, second, twain, [phrase] twelfth, [phrase] twelve, [phrase] twenty (sixscore) thousand, twice, two.

H8148.definition:
from H8150 (שָׁנַן);
something pointed, i.e. a gibe
KJV: byword, taunt.

H8149.definition:
or שְׂנִיר; from an unused root meaning to be pointed; peak;
Shenir or Senir, a summit of Lebanon
KJV: Senir, Shenir.

H8150.definition:
a primitive root;
to point (transitive or intransitive); intensively, to pierce; figuratively, to inculcate
KJV: prick, sharp(-en), teach diligently, whet.

H8151.definition:
a primitive root;
to compress (with a belt)
KJV: gird up.

H8152.definition:
