to plunder
KJV: destroyer, rob, spoil(-er).

H8155.definition:
a primitive root;
to plunder
KJV: rifle, spoil.

H8156.definition:
a primitive root;
to split or tear; figuratively, to upbraid
KJV: cleave, (be) cloven (footed), rend, stay.

H8157.definition:
from H8156 (שָׁסַע);
a fissure
KJV: cleft, clovenfooted.

H8158.definition:
a primitive root;
to cut in pieces, i.e. slaughter
KJV: hew in pieces.

H8159.definition:
a primitive root;
to gaze at or about (properly, for help); by implication, to inspect, consider, compassionate, be nonplussed (as looking around in amazement) or bewildered
KJV: depart, be dim, be dismayed, look (away), regard, have respect, spare, turn.

H8160.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H8159 (שָׁעָה);
properly, a look, i.e. a moment
KJV: hour.

H8161.definition:
feminine from an unused root meaning to stamp;
a clatter (of hoofs)
KJV: stamping.

H8162.definition:
probably of foreign derivation;
linsey-woolsey, i.e. cloth of linen and wool carded and spun together
KJV: garment of divers sorts, linen and wollen.

H8163.definition:
or שָׂעִר; from H8175 (שָׂעַר);
shaggy; as noun, a he-goat; by analogy, a faun
KJV: devil, goat, hairy, kid, rough, satyr.

H8164.definition:
formed the same as H8163 (שָׂעִיר);
a shower (as tempestuous)
KJV: small rain.

H8165.definition:
formed like H8163 (שָׂעִיר); rough;
Seir, a mountain of Idumaea and its aboriginal occupants, also one in Palestine
KJV: Seir.

H8166.definition:
feminine of H8163 (שָׂעִיר);
a she-goat
KJV: kid.

H8167.definition:
formed as H8166 (שְׂעִירָה); roughness;
Seirah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Seirath.

H8168.definition:
from an unused root meaning to hollow out;
the palm; by extension, a handful
KJV: handful, hollow of the hand.

H8169.definition:
or שַׁעֲלַבִּין; plural from H7776 (שׁוּעָל); fox-holes;
Shaalbim or Shaalabbin, a place in Palestine
KJV: Shaalabbin, Shaalbim.

H8170.definition:
patrial from H8169 (שַׁעַלְבִים);
a Shaalbonite or inhabitant of Shaalbin
KJV: Shaalbonite.

H8171.definition:
plural of H7776 (שׁוּעָל); foxes;
Shaalim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Shalim.

H8172.definition:
a primitive root;
to support one's self
KJV: lean, lie, rely, rest (on, self), stay.

H8173.definition:
a primitive root;
(in a good acceptation) to look upon (with complacency), i.e. fondle, please or amuse (self); (in a bad one) to look about (in dismay), i.e. stare
KJV: cry (out) (by confusion with H7768 (שָׁוַע)), dandle, delight (self), play, shut.

H8174.definition:
from H5586 (סָעַף); fluctuation;
Shaaph, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Shaaph.

H8175.definition:
a primitive root;
to storm; by implication, to shiver, i.e. fear
KJV: be (horribly) afraid, fear, hurl as a storm, be tempestuous, come like (take away as with) a whirlwind.

H8177.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H8181 (שֵׂעָר);
hair
KJV: hair.

H8178.definition:
from H8175 (שָׂעַר);
a tempest; also a terror
KJV: affrighted, [idiom] horribly, [idiom] sore, storm. See H8181 (שֵׂעָר).

H8179.definition:
from H8176 (שָׁעַר) in its original sense;
an opening, i.e. door or gate
KJV: city, door, gate, port ([idiom] -er).

H8180.definition:
from H8176 (שָׁעַר);
a measure (as a section)
KJV: (hundred-) fold.

H8181.definition:
or שַׂעַר; (Isaiah 7:20), from H8175 (שָׂעַר) in the sense of dishevelling;
hair (as if tossed or bristling)
KJV: hair(-y), [idiom] rough.

H8182.definition:
from H8176 (שָׁעַר);
harsh or horrid, i.e. offensive
KJV: vile.

H8183.definition:
feminine of H8178 (שַׂעַר);
a hurricane
KJV: storm, tempest.

H8184.definition:
or שְׂעוֹרָה (feminine meaning the plant); and (masculine meaning the grain); also שְׂעֹר; or שְׂעוֹר; from H8175 (שָׂעַר) in the sense of roughness;
barley (as villose)
KJV: barley.

H8185.definition:
feminine of H8181 (שֵׂעָר);
hairiness
KJV: hair.

H8186.definition:
or שַׁעֲרִירִיָּה; or שַׁעֲרֻרִת; feminine from H8176 (שָׁעַר) in the sense of H8175 (שָׂעַר);
something fearful
KJV: horrible thing.

H8187.definition:
from H8176 (שָׁעַר) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has stormed;
Shearjah, an Israelite
KJV: Sheariah.

H8188.definition:
masculine plural of H8184 (שְׂעֹרָה); barley grains;
Seorim, an Israelite
KJV: Seorim.

H8189.definition:
dual of H8179 (שַׁעַר); double gates;
Shaarajim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Shaaraim.

H8190.definition:
of Persian derivation;
Shaashgaz, a eunuch of Xerxes
KJV: Shaashgaz.

H8191.definition:
from H8173 (שָׁעַע);
enjoyment
KJV: delight, pleasure.

H8192.definition:
a primitive root;
to abrade, i.e. bare
KJV: high, stick out.

H8193.definition:
or (in dual and plural) שֶׂפֶת; probably from H5595 (סָפָה) or H8192 (שָׁפָה) through the idea of termination (compare H5490 (סוֹף));
the lip (as a natural boundary); by implication, language; by analogy, a margin (of a vessel, water, cloth, etc.)
KJV: band, bank, binding, border, brim, brink, edge, language, lip, prating, (sea-)shore, side, speech, talk, (vain) words.

H8194.definition:
from H8192 (שָׁפָה) in the sense of clarifying;
a cheese (as strained from the whey)
KJV: cheese.

H8195.definition:
or שְׁפִי; from H8192 (שָׁפָה); baldness (compare H8205 (שְׁפִי));
Shepho or Shephi, an Idumaean
KJV: Shephi, Shepho.

H8196.definition:
or שְׁפוּט; from H8199 (שָׁפַט);
a judicial sentence, i.e. punishment
KJV: judgment.

H8197.definition:
or שְׁפוּפָן; from the same as H8207 (שְׁפִיפֹן); serpent-like;
Shephupham or Shephuphan, an Israelite
KJV: Shephuphan, Shupham.

H8198.definition:
feminine from an unused root meaning to spread out (as a family; see H4940 (מִשְׁפָּחָה));
a female slave (as a member of the household)
KJV: (bond-, hand-) maid(-en, -servant), wench, bondwoman, womanservant.

H8199.definition:
a primitive root;
to judge, i.e. pronounce sentence (for or against); by implication, to vindicate or punish; by extenssion, to govern; passively, to litigate (literally or figuratively)
KJV: [phrase] avenge, [idiom] that condemn, contend, defend, execute (judgment), (be a) judge(-ment), [idiom] needs, plead, reason, rule.
